40:25.265814 Updated by:curator  | non-replicating, recombinant adeno-associated serotype 9 (AAV9) based vector containing the cDNA of the R169Q variant of the human SGSH gene under the control of the murine small nuclear RNA promoter U1a\nSponsor  | Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc\nFunder Type  | Industry\nRecruitment Status  | Recruiting (Click here for study contact information)\nEnrollment Count  | 36 (ESTIMATED)\nResults Posted  | Not Available\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFayuvi (rebisufligene etisparvovec-hopf) FDA Approval History - Drugs.com (https://www.drugs.com/history/fayuvi.html?hash2=%5Bhash2%2Cfallback%3D%5D)\nciteturn186search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; FDA Approved: Yes (First approved September 17, 2026) ... Sep 17, 2026  | Approval FDA Approves Fayuvi (rebisufligene etisparvovec-hopf) Gene Therapy for the Treatment for Sanfilippo Syndrome Type A (MPS IIIA) ... Jul 11, 2025  | Ultragenyx Receives Complete Response Letter from FDA for UX111 AAV Gene Therapy to Treat Sanfilippo Syndrome Type A (MPS IIIA)\n\n# Fayuvi FDA Approval History\n\nLast updated by Judith Stewart, BPharm on Sep 18, 2026.\n\nFDA Approved: Yes (First approved September 17, 2026)\nBrand name: Fayuvi\nGeneric name: rebisufligene etisparvovec-hopf\nDosage form: Suspension for Intravenous Infusion\nPrevious Name: UX111\nCompany: Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc.\nTreatment for: Mucopolysaccharidosis Type IIIA\n\nFayuvi (rebisufligene etisparvovec-hopf) is an adeno-associated virus (AAV) vector-based gene therapy for the treatment of mucopolysaccharidosis type IIIA (MPS IIIA, Sanfilippo Syndrome Type A).\n\n  * Fayuvi is indicated for the treatment of neurologic manifestations of mucopolysaccharidosis type IIIA in pediatric patients with preserved neurodevelopmental function.\n  * Mucopolysaccharidosis type IIIA is a rare, fatal lysosomal storage disease characterized by rapid neurodegeneration, with onset in early childhood. It is caused by biallelic pathogenic variants in the SGSH gene that lead to a deficiency in the sulfamidase (SGSH) enzyme. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFAYUVI FDA Approval: Approved Sep 17, 2026 | pdufa.bio (https://www.pdufa.bio/drug/fayuvi)\nciteturn186search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 days ago; Crawled: yesterday; The FDA approved FAYUVI on Sep 17, 2026. ... Approval record: Standard full approval on September 17, 2026, two days before the September 19 PDUFA goal date; the first FDA-approved treatment for Sanfilippo syndrome type A and Ultragenyx's second gene therapy approval. ... UX111 (ABO-102) was licensed from Abeona Therapeutics (ABEO).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUX111 Gene Therapy (Fayuvi) | MPS IIIA | Phase I-II-III | Ultragenyx (https://curesanfilippofoundation.org/2020/03/abo-102-gene-therapy-sanfilippo-type-iiia/)\nciteturn186search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.7 years ago; Crawled: today; #### September 2026 ... 17, 2026, FDA granted standard full approval of FAYUVI™, rebisufligene etisparvovec-hopf (known as UX111).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNational MPS Society Responds: UX111 Decision (https://mpssociety.org/en/news/fayuvi-ux111-approval/)\nciteturn186search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: today; # The Wait Is Over: FDA Approves Fayuvi (UX111), the First-Ever Treatment for Sanfilippo Syndrome Type A\n\n## September 17, 2026 ... Food and Drug Administration’s approval of Fayuvi, or UX111 (rebisufligene etisparvovec), the first-ever approved treatment, and the first gene therapy, for Mucopolysaccharidosis Type IIIA (Sanfilippo syndrome Type A).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRARE FDA decision: FAYUVI (UX111), Approved September 17, 2026 | pdufa.bio (https://www.pdufa.bio/pdufa/RARE-u